This is my second ascension; the first being a Wiz-Gno-Fem-Neu back in June.
After taking 18 months of YASDs to ascend my first, I'm very happy to have
cut that time by 1/3.

As is pretty common, I don't seen to recall much of the early game. I do
remember several bones files from Hearse that didn't give me much in
quality, but definitely added to the quantity of items I had available.
Excalibur was acquired at Exp LVL 5, quickly enchanted up to +7. An early
spellbook of charm monster was also fortunate, as was the magic whistle
found not long afterward. If I recall correctly, I picked up a ring of slow
digestion pretty early, as well.

If I recall, Minetown was my first conquest, providing me with a silver
saber and little else. I #twoweaponed from this point out. The rest of the
mines was forgettable, although I did come across a BOH (always helpful).
Sokoban was next, again quite forgettable, but fortunately I came away with
the Amulet of Reflection. I was quite happy about that.

>From there, Fort Ludios was next. With the +7 Excalibur and +7 silver saber,
the Fort fell easily. I came away with BlackDSM, which was much, much better
than what I had been using. All treasure then went to the Priest on a nearby
level, getting my AC down to a respectable level. The castle was also an
easy conquest. The wand of wishing was used to acquire SDSM, a helm of
brilliance, gauntlets of dexterity, a magic marker, and an amulet of life
saving. Two wishes were wasted (one for Greyswandir, which was denied; and
one for a spellbook of Finger of Death, which I never could fully use).

One frustrating point was that I never managed to get a better weapon than
Excalibur. I did receive Sunsword from my God, but also Ogresmasher, Fire
Brand, and Cleaver. Blecch. I also was crowned very early, as well.

At this point I went and completed the Quest. I was pretty powerful at this
point, and I took out the Minion in 3 turns. Almost anti-climactic.

Gehennom was my next destination- I breezed through hell as well. Juiblex,
Asmodeus Orcus, Baalzebub and Geyron were defeated easily. Vlad went down
even easier- getting the Candelabrum and the Amulet of Life Saving (my 2nd)
was a mere formality. I trogged down to the bottom, located the vibrating
square, and then I want back to my stash in the castle to reorganize and
relearn my spells. Heading back down, I woke up Rodney (very rudely, with a
wand of death, I might add), grabbed the Book, and went for the Amulet. The
high priest was dispatched with my wand as well, and for only my second
time, I had the Amulet!

I got knocked back quite a few times, was visited by Rodney more than I
would have like to have been (17 times!), but eventually managed to reach
the Planes. The Planes weren't nearly as hair-raising as my first time
through- actually seemed to go faster this time.

Reaching the Astral Plane, I decided to go right and visit Famine first.
Fighting my way through the masses, things seemed to be under control.
Angels, priests, insects all fell before me. I noticed that a Ranger (or was
it a Rogue?) was approaching- I didn't think much of it... until I see
something about my amulet growing warm.... Huh? What the? He had Vorpal
Blade? You've GOT to be kidding me! Needless to say, after being decapitated
once, and only having one more Amulet of Life Saving, I went into panic
mode. I dispatched the bugger with my wand of death, grabbed that Blade,
then rushed to the altar. Neutral?! Ugh! Back through the fray, still in
panic mode, I went to visit Death in the middle. I recklessly hacked and
slashed my way to the altar, only to find out it was again the wrong one. At
this point, having fought past Death and his companions with no regards to
my own health, I realized that I was going to need my second Amulet of LS,
and very soon. At this point, I realized that I wasn't quite in the right
mindset- I wasn't thinking things through, only hacking/slashing, I decided
to quit for the day. Upon returning to the game, resolute to the fact I had
run out of chances, I went through my inventory, prepared everything I
thought I'd need (including recharging my wands of death, and swapping my
ring of free action for regeneration), died again (it was a matter of time),
then went after the last altar. I dispatched Pestilence, danced thorough
attackers, and finally reached the altar.

And here I am. Whew!

